 "type": "skill"}]}], "id": 11, "stimuli_ids": []}], "stimuli": [{"template_override": 1, "_data": [], "type": "welcome", "contents": [{}], "id": 0}, {"template_override": 1, "_data": [], "type": "audio", "title": "", "contents": [{"type": "slideshow", "value": {"audiosrc": "engenn10le02ob09re2aud01", "coverimg": "engenn10le02ob09re2img01.jpg", "images": [{"image": "engenn10le02ob09re2img01.jpg", "text": "", "time": "0", "id": 0}, {"image": "engenn10le02ob09re2img01.jpg", "text": "Bungee jumping is an exhilarating sport which involves tying strong elastic cords to one's ankles and leaping from a high place like a tower or a bridge.\n</br>\nThe origins of bungee jumping can be traced to Pentecost Island in the South Pacific. Teenage boys proved they had reached manhood by tying vines to their ankles and jumping off specially-built towers. It must have been seen as a rite of passage in which they faced their fears just like their forefathers did in years gone by. After the jump, there was a gratifying celebration for all the inhabitants of the island with special ceremonies and a festive banquet. Satisfied parents would look on with pride as their sons were glorified. Bungee jumping might have been introduced to the western world by Captain James Cook, who discovered Pentecost Island in 1770. To this day, some of the best jumps in the world may be enjoyed from these cliffs.", "time": "100", "id": 1}, {"image": "engenn10le02ob09re2img02.jpg", "text": "In the past fifteen years, bungee jumping has found widespread success in America, Europe, and Australia. This may have been caused by increased accessibility. The way bungee jumpers enjoy their diversion has changed, though. They still jump from cliffs just as the original creators of the sport intended. But nowadays those looking for a more thrilling challenge also jump from special towers and even hot air balloons, from altitudes up to 150 feet (46 meters) above the ground. A free fall from that height must be quite an unsettling feeling!", "time": "55000", "id": 2}, {"image": "engenn10le02ob09re2img03.jpg", "text": "In order to minimize the dangers, a jumper ought to be accompanied by an experienced partner, and a safety code, like that of the British bungee association,  must be followed by all licensed bungee jumping clubs.", "time": "91950", "id": 3}]}}], "id": 1}], "type": "scholar", "id": 0, "_data": [{"type": "lab_options", "contents": [{"content": true, "type": "has_nav"}, {"content": true, "type": "has_exercise_controls"}]}]}], "type": "sena"}